      ":question/id": "49bb4710-b92e-54c7-b99c-2722f73c1b5c",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -4 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -4 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -4 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot."
