      ":question/id": "4edefd5c-4505-5968-9bc4-0b2aa552a2d8",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z&=4 \\\\ -x+y-3z&=0 \\\\ x+3z&=4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot."
